PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
DATABASE_URL=paste-your-supabase-string-here
JWT_SECRET=paste-a-long-random-text-here
ADMIN_EMAIL=youremail@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=YourNewPassword123
TRUST_PROXY=0
Replace each value:
DATABASE_URL: your Supabase Session pooler string, with your real password in place of [YOUR-PASSWORD].
JWT_SECRET: any random text of 32 or more characters. You can create one by running this in the terminal and pasting the result:
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
ADMIN_PASSWORD: 10 or more characters, with upper case, lower case and a number